# v53 — decode launch bounds

## Differential audit finding
Original CUTLASS instantiates kernels with explicit static threadblock shapes and resource expectations. The current 256-thread v51 decode kernel has no launch-bounds contract, so nvcc may choose a register allocation that reduces resident blocks or fails to expose the intended occupancy tradeoff.

## Single hypothesis
Add __launch_bounds__(256, 2) to only 	hree_level_decode_kernel, requesting at least two resident 256-thread blocks per SM while letting nvcc adjust registers accordingly. No data, arithmetic, precision, mapping, model or benchmark setting changes.

## Falsification criteria
Any correctness failure rejects v53. If correctness passes but speedup is not above v51, restore v51.
